# What does not go into an image build.
#
# Thirty Dockerfiles build from this directory as their context, and a context is
# sent to the daemon in full before the first COPY is read. Without this file
# that meant .git — half a gigabyte, and the gate clones it in full because the
# schema upgrade test needs the history — and ml/target, a gigabyte of Rust
# build output, thirty times over.
#
# It lists what is not in any image rather than what is, because the failure of
# the other arrangement is silent: a new directory nobody adds to the allow list
# is one the build cannot see, and the error arrives as a missing package.
.git
.github
backups
secrets

# The ML tier is its own language and its own image. It builds from ./ml with
# its own .dockerignore, so excluding it here costs those images nothing and
# keeps it out of the thirty that do not use it.
ml

# Left behind by a test run or a build in a service directory. Neither is copied
# by any Dockerfile, and both are large.
e2e/provision
services/*/server
services/*/cmd/server/server
